# Gapless fast path, part 1 of 6: hook the decoder reset-and-start choke point.
name: gapless-1-gate-hook
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x0306cb2c
gate: build refuses unless the 4 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: 0x0306cb2c is the reset-and-start routine for core-1 decoder
  modules (assert reset line, image load via 0x03067870 with flags 7,
  parameter-page copy, ready poll). A BL-target scan of all 82 modules
  shows exactly ten call sites, all in module 33's per-codec dispatcher
  (0x0308886e cases) -- this entry is the single choke point every
  decoder load passes through, for every codec. The patch replaces the
  routine's first two instructions (`push {r4,r5,r6,lr}`; `mov r5, r0`,
  4 bytes total) with a B.W to the gate cave at 0x03051664 (0022). The
  cave re-executes both displaced instructions before deciding, and its
  stock path branches back to 0x0306cb30, the instruction after the
  hook, so the stock body runs unchanged whenever the fast path does
  not fire (which includes every build without the ARM patch 0026).
expect: 70b50546
replace: e4f79abd
